# Private research/source materials -- literature PDFs, internal research
# summaries, and any other local-only documents. Never tracked, regardless
# of what subfolder structure gets added under here later.
Source/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Segmentation/ (root/segmentation phase, moved into its own top-level
# folder 2026-07-29). Patterns below are anchored to wherever this
# .gitignore file lives (git treats any pattern containing a "/" in the
# middle as anchored to the .gitignore's own directory, not matched at any
# depth) -- so they need the Segmentation/ prefix explicitly, or the
# large binaries they're meant to exclude would silently become
# trackable again after the move. Single-segment patterns (no "/" in the
# middle, e.g. archive.zip, venv/, __pycache__/) match at any depth
# regardless and did not need changing.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Raw dataset archive
archive.zip
dataset anemia/

# Locally-kept full-output backups of the notebooks/*_full_visual_audit.ipynb
# review notebooks (each 90MB+ once actually run, with embedded per-patient
# image overlays) -- the tracked notebook files themselves are always kept
# output-stripped/clean; these backups exist purely so a personal review run
# isn't lost, and must never be swept into a commit.
Segmentation/notebooks/*_executed_backup.ipynb

# Processed image/mask outputs (large binaries, regenerable from archive.zip)
Segmentation/data/processed/images/
Segmentation/data/processed/masks/

# Raw-photo-aligned image/mask outputs (large binaries, regenerable via
# Segmentation/scripts/build_aligned_dataset.py; alignment_log.csv is NOT
# ignored -- it's small and worth keeping in version control)
Segmentation/data/processed/aligned_raw/images/
Segmentation/data/processed/aligned_raw/masks/

# Same, for the forniceal_palpebral tissue-type variant
# (Segmentation/scripts/build_aligned_dataset_forniceal.py)
Segmentation/data/processed/aligned_raw_forniceal/images/
Segmentation/data/processed/aligned_raw_forniceal/masks/

# Orphaned local output from the abandoned Phase 3 crop-based approach
# (its generating scripts were deleted; this directory is stale disk
# clutter, kept ignored purely so it can't be accidentally committed)
Segmentation/data/cropped/

# Python virtual environment
venv/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local backups / Kaggle upload-prep artifacts (left at repo root, not
# moved into Segmentation/ -- they're stale pre-reorg directory snapshots)
clean_map.txt
folder_map.txt
folder_map_utf8.txt
Segmentation/data/processed/eyes_processed_data.zip
Segmentation/data/processed/aligned_raw.zip
Segmentation/data/processed/aligned_raw_forniceal.zip

# Trained model checkpoints (large binaries, regenerable by retraining;
# outputs/logs/ metrics CSV/JSON are NOT ignored -- those are small and
# worth keeping in version control)
Segmentation/outputs/checkpoints/
classification/outputs/plots/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-08-11 after ~9GB of checkpoint/zip binaries got accidentally
# committed (swept into a broad `git add` alongside unrelated work) and
# had to be manually stripped from history before ever reaching GitHub --
# see Segmentation/.project_memory/05_kfold_reevaluation.md and
# 03_tech_stack_and_rules.md's git-safety rules for the full account.
# Same convention as above: checkpoints/zips ignored, logs/plots (small)
# stay trackable.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Manually-downloaded/extracted Kaggle sweep results (project author's own
# local copy of the real training run output, not generated by any script
# in this repo, folder-naming inconsistent by hand -- e.g. "results base"
# vs "results_mid"). Checkpoints (multi-hundred-MB .pth each) and the
# zip archives Kaggle produces are the large parts; logs/plots stay tracked.
Segmentation/scripts/train_pretrained/output/*/checkpoints/
Segmentation/scripts/train_pretrained/output/*/*.zip

# classification/new_way's own trained checkpoints (same large-binary
# class of file as Segmentation/outputs/checkpoints/ above, just a
# different module -- logs/ under the same Output/ dir stays tracked).
# Wildcarded 2026-08-12 (same fix as the Segmentation pattern above, same
# reason): Output/ was reorganized into Output/version1/, Output/version2/
# subfolders, and the old literal .../Output/checkpoints/ path stopped
# matching either -- verified via git check-ignore that BOTH version1/
# and version2/'s checkpoints were silently unignored before this fix.
classification/new_way/Output/*/checkpoints/

# classification/new_way/Fine_tune/'s own checkpoints -- same large-binary class, different
# module again (2026-08-13's partial fine-tuning pilot programme). These are full fp32 state
# dicts (no fp16 downcast, unlike new_way/kfold/'s checkpoints), 335MB-625MB each, ~1.4GB total
# across the 5 saved here -- verified uncovered by any existing pattern (git check-ignore) before
# this was added, i.e. a broad `git add` would have committed all 1.4GB without this entry.
classification/new_way/Fine_tune/Output/checkpoints/

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Added 2026-08-12, project author's explicit request: internal working-
# memory notes should stay local-only, not published to GitHub. Previously
# these were deliberately tracked (CLAUDE.md's own session-start
# instruction pointed at Segmentation/.project_memory/*.md), so this is a
# reversal of that earlier convention, not an oversight -- untracked via
# `git rm --cached`, not deleted, so local content is unaffected.
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
/memory/
Segmentation/.project_memory/
classification/.project_memory/


